      "message": "\u003e Separately: unparking before parked.addAll(notReady) re-adds the not-ready tasks leaves a brief window where they\u0027re absent from parked. Since updateParked() isn\u0027t synchronized and the unparked task\u0027s onStop() can re-enter it, the old ordering (parked.addAll() then ready.unpark()) seems safer here. Was the reorder deliberate?\n\nThe reordering was deliberate as it simplifies the code. There is indeed a race there, and I guess your concern is that this makes the race a bit longer? I don\u0027t know if it actually does, because I suspect the compiler can re-order those as it wishes anyway. As you probably are aware, the intent was to address the race in this series: https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/gerrit/+/442764 which may need to be re-checked if it still makes sense based on all the changes since it was created.",
